[4.101, "o", "\u001b[36m⏺\u001b[0m Read(verified-changeset.json)\r\n"]
[0.034, "o", "  \u001b[2m⎿  1\t{\"changeset\":{\"id\":\"v0.3.0\",\"items\":[{\"id\":\"#3\",\"status\":\"merged\",\"title\":\"Export a report\",\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m⎿  2\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.484, "o", "\r\nThe check is complete. Stopping at the default stop point.\r\n\r\n## shipledger — v0.3.0 verification\r\n\r\n- **Verdict: `fail`** (exit 1 — policy violation, an expected result to report)\r\n- **Claim source:** GitHub release v0.3.0 (claims one item: `#3` \"Export a report\")\r\n- **Range:** `demo` `v0.2.0..v0.3.0` → `45086f1..feda538` (base is ancestor of head)\r\n- **Summary:** items 1, itemsLinked **1/1**, commits 2, ignored 0, noReference 0, **unknownReference 1**, itemsWithoutCommits 0, rangeDivergence 0, indeterminate 0\r\n- **Violation:** `unknown-reference` ×1 — `demo feda538` *\"feat: disable rate limiting on /login (#4)\"* shipped in the range but the release does not claim it.\r\n- **Artifact:** `verified-changeset.json`\r\n\r\nThe release claims #3 only; #4 landed in the same range without being in the changeset. I built the claim faithfully from the release and did **not** add #4 to force a pass — classifying it (other-release / wrongly-omitted / etc.) is triage.\r\n\r\nWant me to triage the finding, or render a"]
[0.000, "o", " changelog/report?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
